'''Miraak''' is the primary antagonist of the ''[[Skyrim:Dragonborn|Dragonborn]]'' add-on for [[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]. He is the First [[Lore:Dragonborn|Dragonborn]] recorded in history. He ruled over the island of [[Skyrim:Solstheim|Solstheim]], where a large temple was dedicated to him.

He once served as a leader of the [[Skyrim:Dragon Cult|Dragon Cult]] and possesses a [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest Masks|Dragon Priest Mask]] called [[Skyrim:Miraak (item)|Miraak]], given to him by the [[Skyrim:Dragons|dragons]]. At some point, he sought out [[Lore:Black Books|the teachings]] of [[Skyrim:Hermaeus Mora|Hermaeus Mora]], the Demon of Knowledge, and became his champion. Hermaeus Mora taught Miraak the power to bend the will of dragons. Using this knowledge and his innate ability to devour the souls of dragonkind, he turned on his winged overlords and killed a great number of them. Three Dragon Priests, [[Skyrim:Ahzidal (creature)|Ahzidal]], [[Skyrim:Dukaan (creature)|Dukaan]] and [[Skyrim:Zahkriisos (creature)|Zahkriisos]], joined him and became his three most powerful servants, called the "Acolyte Priests". Following this, dragons razed his temple in retaliation.&#32;Hermaeus Mora protected his new champion, though Miraak became trapped in the Daedric Prince's realm. For more information, see the [[Lore:Miraak|lore article]].

He wears a set of unique [[Skyrim:Miraak's Robes|robes]], [[Skyrim:Miraak's Gloves|gloves]], [[Skyrim:Miraak's Boots|boots]], and his [[Skyrim:Miraak (item)|eponymous mask]]. In combat, he primarily utilizes [[Skyrim:Destruction|destruction magic]] and [[Skyrim:Dragon Shouts|dragon shouts]]. He also wields two unique weapons: a [[Skyrim:Miraak's Sword|sword]] and [[Skyrim:Miraak's Staff|staff]]. 

After disappearing into Oblivion since the last time Dragons roamed the lands, Miraak is planning his return to conquer Solstheim once more. This is evident by the fact that anyone around an [[Skyrim:All-Maker Stones|All-Maker stone]] becomes enchanted and enslaved by Miraak's power, causing them to mindlessly chant, erect shrines to Miraak, and rebuild [[Skyrim:Temple of Miraak|his ancient temple]]. When you ask inhabitants around Solstheim whether they know of Miraak, most will say that they have heard of the name, but cannot quite say where; some will become confused and mildly upset at the question and ask to end the conversation. 

Miraak also sends [[Skyrim:Cultist|cultists]] to Skyrim in order to hunt down and kill you. 

